join ember (normal) right [animation="Fade In"]
ember: You came back!
ember: I half-expected yesterday to scare you off, honestly.
ember: How are you holding up?
[wait time="0.1"]
- Every second was worth it.
	ember (smug): Okay, now you're just trying to make me blush. (+20 Charm)
	[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"charm":20}"]
	ember: Is that a tactic, or do you actually mean it?
	- Both, honestly.
		ember: At least you're honest about the tactic part. (+10 Charm)
		[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"charm":10}"]
	- I mean it. No tactics.
		ember: Okay. I believe you. (+10 Trust)
		[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"trust":10}"]
- Educational. I learned a lot about doubt, mostly.
	ember: Ha! Yeah, that one doesn't quit, does it. (+20 Wit)
	[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"wit":20}"]
	ember: Did it get to you at all? Be honest.
	- A little. Didn't stop me though.
		ember: That's really all I can ask for. (+10 Trust)
		[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"trust":10}"]
	- Not even a little. I had it handled.
		ember: Confident. I like that. (+10 Charm)
		[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"charm":10}"]
- I just wanted to make sure you were okay.
	ember: That means more to me than you'd think. (+20 Trust)
	[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"trust":20}"]
	ember: Not everyone checks in like that. Why do you?
	- Because it matters to me that you're okay.
		ember (sad): Okay. That's... a lot, in a good way. (Vulnerability risk)
		do GameManager.apply_vulnerability_risk(10, 0.6)
		if {last_vulnerability_success} == true:
			ember: I don't say this often, but — thank you. Really.
		else:
			ember (sad): I don't really know what to do with someone saying that. Give me a second.
	- Habit, I guess. I look out for people.
		ember: A good habit to have. (+10 Trust)
		[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"trust":10}"]
ember: Anyway. I have a feeling today won't be any quieter than yesterday.
ember: Ready?
do GameManager.end_dialauge()